#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:53
msgid ""
"SS buffers have static shapes, uint32/uint64 elements, and 32-byte aligned "
"allocation bases within the MIX 1:2 group's 3 KiB SS pool. Allocation does "
"not initialize the contents. ``T.view`` may reinterpret the same storage. SS "
"follows ordinary buffer optimization semantics; unused accesses may be "
"removed. Synchronization establishes publication and slot-reuse order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:59
msgid ""
"The two AIVs must write disjoint byte ranges. AIV/AIC dependencies use "
"ordinary automatic cross-core synchronization. Direct AIV peer dependencies "
"require explicit synchronization, as with other shared storage. Manual "
"kernels must supply their own publication and slot-reuse protocol. Automatic "
"multibuffering uses the same ownership and version annotations as L1. All "
"views share one version clock; every version counts toward the group's 3072-"
"byte capacity. SS is scalar-only: VF access, DMA and atomics are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:73
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:81
msgid ""
"Layout is deferred to the consuming gemm operation, which infers K-major or "
"MN-major from its transpose flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:91
msgid "Memory scope. Defaults to \"shared.l0c\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:92
msgid "Whether to annotate the fixed Ascend L0C accumulator layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:99
msgid ""
"The handle (scope ``shared.l0a.sf``) materializes no storage: the hardware "
"keys a tile's scale slots to the tile's own address. Load scales with "
"``T.copy(sf_l1, handle)`` and pass the handle to ``T.gemm_blockscaled`` as "
"``SFA``. Allocation permanently binds this handle to ``buf``; GEMM verifies "
"the binding and leading indices. Scale slots are sticky, so one scale load "
"may serve several data loads (see testing/ascend/language/"
"test_tilelang_ascend_mx_sf_slots.py)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:107
msgid ""
"The default shape preserves all leading dimensions and assumes trailing "
"untransposed ``(rows, K)`` matrix dimensions with one scale per 32 K "
"elements packed into ``sf_dtype`` (``uint16`` = one pair per 64 K elements); "
"pass ``sf_shape`` explicitly for transposed tiles. Allocate one SF handle "
"per data buffer and reuse that handle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/allocate/index.rst:118
msgid "See :func:`alloc_l0a_sf`; identical semantics for the L0B slot shadow."
msgstr ""
